  "review_scope": "Skate one-shots now play through owned spatial audio components, created by the same factory as SpawnSoundAtLocation, so per-voice gain and a 3000 Hz low-pass reach voices already playing. Loops multiply their unchanged envelope by the skate gain; at the default gain of one the product equals the previous envelope, and LoadSounds enables the filter only when softening is already on. EndPlay additionally stops owned one-shots. Cue choice, variant bookkeeping, speed/pitch curves, attenuation and timing are unchanged, so the offline skate profile still represents the default unfiltered mix. Footstep ApplyVoicePreferences now also sets the component's low-pass properties, which Play copies; the engine setters alone reach only an already-active sound, so new footsteps were never filtered. Footstep emission bodies are unchanged. No new hardware listening or bit-identical output is claimed."
